+# Agent Note: Public selection-aware composer text insertion
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-05-public-composer-text-insertion.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Session-scoped Slot components receive the stable `InputActions` face, but that face could only replace the whole draft or submit it. A feature that needed to insert plain text at the current selection therefore had to destroy the draft through `setDraft`, reach into the private `ComposerKeyboard.paste` face, or manipulate Lexical/DOM state outside the owning package.
+
+## Decision
+
+`InputActions` exposes one additional synchronous operation, `insertText(text: string): void`. `SessionInputShell.actions` delegates it to the shell's existing paste implementation, so public insertion strips forged reference placeholders, replaces the current range selection, falls back to the document end without a selection, preserves untouched rich nodes, and carries `PASTE_TAG` as one undo boundary.
+
+The new action exposes no editor, selection object, Lexical node, or span coordinate; `ComposerKeyboard` remains private to [`ui-conversation`](../../../../packages/client/ui-conversation/README.md). The public operation accepts plain text only and adds no options, return status, selection handle, or submit behavior.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Expose `ComposerKeyboard.paste`.** That face also carries editor identity, keyboard arbitration, trigger completion, and explicit submit modes. Publishing it would couple feature plugins to InputBar event-handler behavior instead of exposing the one supported edit.
+
+**Compose `useInput().draft` with `setDraft`.** Rebuilding the projected string loses the current selection and can flatten reference-chip identity, so it cannot satisfy selection-aware insertion.
+
+**Add options or return a success flag.** The current consumer requires exactly the established paste behavior, and valid insertion has no asynchronous admission result. Additional modes would create a second editing policy without a consumer.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Session-scoped Slot features can insert safe plain text without receiving editor internals.
+- Clipboard paste and programmatic insertion share sanitization, selection fallback, rich-node preservation, and undo behavior, so fixes remain local to one implementation.
+- The operation does not submit, insert rich nodes, expose selection coordinates, or report whether placeholder-only input became a no-op.
+- `packages/client/ui-conversation/tests/input-actions.client.spec.ts` exercises the public face over range selection, absent selection, placeholder sanitization, no-op publication, undo, and preserved reference chips.
